nd, and folding is too conservative for the potential of JTs.\n\nReason: JTs is a premium drawing hand with high implied odds. Calling the opponent\'s raise allows you to see the community cards and realize your equity without overcommitting chips pre-flop.\n\nAnswer: 0'}
